[[1740,668,"Poor record keeping in regard to key areas of care namely falls and wound management and handover information on discharge A failure to understand or to follow use of aseptic techniques and cleanliness when managing wounds thus increasing the risk of infection","inadequate documentation of falls and wound care",""],[4536,1714,"Failure of members of staff to understand the concept of confirmation bias","confirmation bias",""],[4537,1714,"A reluctance on the part of staff to accept situations of confirmation bias and be open to altering practices","staff reluctance to adapt",""],[4538,1714,"I am not satisfied the Newsletters had been considered and digested by all staff","newsletters not fully considered by staff",""],[4539,1714,"The training program in place is delivered over a 12-month period thus many staff members will not have had that training and there is a risk that confirmation bias situations will continue placing mothers and their babies at risk","delayed training completion",""],[4540,1714,"some staff members who were involved in Clay's management were not prioritised to have that training","excluded staff from bias training",""],[6557,2496,"Failure to document an assessment of Glasgow Coma Score and the result","incomplete Glasgow Coma Score assessment",""],[11858,4568,"clear evidence of poor compliance with the Enhanced Care Supervision engagement policy and daily assessments","poor compliance with Enhanced Care Supervision",""],[11859,4568,"no evidence to suggest that any action was taken by the Trust following escalation by ward staff regarding concerns about the lack of resources to provide appropriate supervision","lack of resources for appropriate supervision",""],[11860,4568,"Secretary of State for Health is asked to consider whether it is appropriate for Trust to review its systems and procedures in place in relation to Enhanced care Supervision","systems and procedures for Enhanced Care Supervision",""],[14567,5693,"Poor communication